OL,3,GNEWSAHummingbird hawk moths and ivy
OL,4,Abees: The insects thriving as
OL,5,Atemperatures rise
OL,6,
OL,7,FAs parts of the West Midlands baked in
OL,8,Fwarmer temperatures this summer,
OL,9,Fspecies once considered unusual in the
OL,10,Fregion, such as hummingbird hawk moths,
OL,11,Fivy bees and the wasp spider have been
OL,12,Fspotted in growing numbers.
OL,14,FThe hummingbird hawk moth, known for
OL,15,Fits furry grey body, orange hindwings
OL,16,Fand long proboscis, migrates to the UK
OL,17,Ffrom southern Europe and north Africa
OL,18,Fin the summer months.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,357,350,200,160,0,100
