OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,$A(W)
OL,3,GNEWSAHummingbird hawk moths and ivy
OL,4,Abees: The insects thriving as
OL,5,Atemperatures rise
OL,6,
OL,7,FJames Benwell, from the Birmingham and
OL,8,FBlack Country Wildlife Trust, said 2026
OL,9,Fwas a "record year" for sightings of
OL,10,Fthe species, which was often mistaken
OL,11,Ffor a small bird.
OL,13,FThe moth, which can be seen hovering
OL,14,Fover flowers, has wings that beat about
OL,15,F80 times per second, according to
OL,16,FBenwell.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
